<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruy González de Clavijo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1412</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruy González de Clavijo was a Castilian courtier sent by King Henry III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> as ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>. Leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1403, he travelled through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> in 1404. His account of the embassy, published as the Embajada a Tamorlán, is a major source on Timur's court and the lands between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ruy-gonzalez-de-clavijo.jpg" alt="Ruy González de Clavijo" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rufino Casado · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_de_Ruy_Gonz%C3%A1lez_de_Clavijo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
